{
    "word": "clamorous",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "d4cf411d-f16e-34a3-9d22-c465b2979718",
                "word": "clamorous",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "fa421bff-af69-4baa-ba91-445a69f43476",
                        "entry_id": "d4cf411d-f16e-34a3-9d22-c465b2979718",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more clamorous"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "29f8a492-1637-4d5a-8903-eaa47c5604bc",
                        "entry_id": "d4cf411d-f16e-34a3-9d22-c465b2979718",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most clamorous"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6eee54cb-ea41-3f91-831d-85e5ec706fd9",
                        "entry_id": "d4cf411d-f16e-34a3-9d22-c465b2979718",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to clamor.",
                            "Of great intensity. (of sounds)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e3d8925-ea4a-4519-a4d0-6c05f153bf0a",
                                "sense_id": "6eee54cb-ea41-3f91-831d-85e5ec706fd9",
                                "text": "a clamorous fire alarm"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b54787ba-b52e-49a1-97ec-0a4fb23cf737",
                                "sense_id": "6eee54cb-ea41-3f91-831d-85e5ec706fd9",
                                "text": "[…] he took the bride about the neck,\nAnd kiss’d her lips with such a clamorous smack\nThat at the parting all the church did echo."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a70ee30b-5c4a-496b-a0f6-d4686f0fe93f",
                                "sense_id": "6eee54cb-ea41-3f91-831d-85e5ec706fd9",
                                "text": "[…] the sound [of laughter] ceased, only for an instant; it began again, louder: for at first, though distinct, it was very low. It passed off in a clamorous peal that seemed to wake an echo in every lonely chamber;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e479d46b-a216-369a-b71f-18bfd5e19390",
                        "entry_id": "d4cf411d-f16e-34a3-9d22-c465b2979718",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to clamor.",
                            "Creating a loud noise. (of people, animals or things)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6ab4882-0c7c-4e37-8c82-85daa86b5b16",
                                "sense_id": "e479d46b-a216-369a-b71f-18bfd5e19390",
                                "text": "clamorous trumpets"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1d1f653-9404-424e-a540-5ef5b051957d",
                                "sense_id": "e479d46b-a216-369a-b71f-18bfd5e19390",
                                "text": "The clamorous owl that nightly hoots"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c378b149-5b93-3beb-ac3d-b2186905b53b",
                        "entry_id": "d4cf411d-f16e-34a3-9d22-c465b2979718",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to clamor.",
                            "Expressed loudly. (of emotions or feelings)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "778a04d8-692b-4fd9-be3f-f2907a2923a8",
                                "sense_id": "c378b149-5b93-3beb-ac3d-b2186905b53b",
                                "text": "We are disgusted with that clamorous grief, which, without any delicacy, calls upon our compassion with sighs and tears and importunate lamentations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d56450ff-4557-4589-b2f8-e6d50847f168",
                                "sense_id": "c378b149-5b93-3beb-ac3d-b2186905b53b",
                                "text": "[…] in the clamorous happiness of Lydia herself in bidding farewell, the more gentle adieus of her sisters were uttered without being heard."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "27ddb0fd-65f7-383e-816f-b0384a1b9e90",
                        "entry_id": "d4cf411d-f16e-34a3-9d22-c465b2979718",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to clamor.",
                            "Filled with or accompanied by a great deal of noise. (of times, places, events or activities)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "741449a0-4552-40ba-a7b7-6d3e332209b2",
                                "sense_id": "27ddb0fd-65f7-383e-816f-b0384a1b9e90",
                                "text": "a clamorous market"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53467102-bffb-46a1-a479-169457774a2c",
                                "sense_id": "27ddb0fd-65f7-383e-816f-b0384a1b9e90",
                                "text": "Life had long been astir in the village, and clamorous labor\nKnocked with its hundred hands at the golden gates of the morning."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65906a7c-0226-436b-9c72-a3879cfa47ef",
                                "sense_id": "27ddb0fd-65f7-383e-816f-b0384a1b9e90",
                                "text": "[…] he tried rising late, but the clamorous dawn, filled with clanging milkmen and argumentative crows, was always victorious."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fe3658a2-afff-39c7-b5e2-6fdf11400625",
                        "entry_id": "d4cf411d-f16e-34a3-9d22-c465b2979718",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to clamor.",
                            "Insistently expressing a desire for something."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of people or speech"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cc68298-245a-4647-87b2-eebddd2916c3",
                                "sense_id": "fe3658a2-afff-39c7-b5e2-6fdf11400625",
                                "text": "Be clamorous and leap all civil bounds\nRather than make unprofited return."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3350f2d2-7075-49e0-ac10-21f17e235940",
                                "sense_id": "fe3658a2-afff-39c7-b5e2-6fdf11400625",
                                "text": "[…] Overbury in the mean time might write clamorous and furious Letters to his Friends,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37bdeee6-96eb-42a3-9c35-f42f0d7201cf",
                                "sense_id": "fe3658a2-afff-39c7-b5e2-6fdf11400625",
                                "text": "The people became clamorous to get land, and the rich and the great, we may believe, were perfectly determined not to give them any part of theirs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49cf199e-9d63-4b88-a2ce-249c359f7613",
                                "sense_id": "fe3658a2-afff-39c7-b5e2-6fdf11400625",
                                "text": "They were clamorous for an expedition to the hills, before the calm stillness of the autumn should be disturbed by storms."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9c4a6d5a-3f04-339b-b3b9-c3eab4638d17",
                        "entry_id": "d4cf411d-f16e-34a3-9d22-c465b2979718",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having especially (and often unpleasantly) bright or contrasting colours or patterns."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d102e87-d638-465d-8694-e61e8b0784c7",
                                "sense_id": "9c4a6d5a-3f04-339b-b3b9-c3eab4638d17",
                                "text": "It was impossible to overlook the clamorous parrots on the new missionary’s Hawaiian shirt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1215c20b-a6f4-46ca-99ce-1e7f0f0f1af9",
                                "sense_id": "9c4a6d5a-3f04-339b-b3b9-c3eab4638d17",
                                "text": "She led them along a path edged with round, whitewashed stones and equally rounded basils of a clamorous green."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bda7ac09-f3bf-42d2-aef6-feb7cc215a1c",
